  "document": "Almonte, Ontario\nAlmonte (pronounced \"AL-mont\" as opposed to the original Spanish pronunciation of \"al-MON-tay\") is a former mill town located in Lanark County, in the eastern portion of Ontario, Canada. Formerly a separate municipality, Almonte is now a ward of the town of Mississippi Mills, which was created on January 1, 1998 by the merging of Almonte with Ramsay and Pakenham townships. Almonte is located 46 km south-west of downtown Ottawa. Its population as of 2013 is about 5,000."
